(7796314, 1299841, 12200, '<td valign="top">
Surprised this one didn''t place higher. It was among my favorites this challenge. The b/w inversion was an imaginative choice that makes this presumably mundane (and probably less-than-picturesque) scene something haunting and, well, mysterious. A real artist''s touch in my book. :-)</td>', 'Surprised this one didn''t place higher. It was among my favorites this challenge. The b/w inversion was an imaginative choice that makes this presumably mundane (and probably less-than-picturesque) scene something haunting and, well, mysterious. A real artist''s touch in my book. :-)', '2025-10-01 13:45:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7796315, 1299362, 12200, '<td valign="top">
Glad to see this one on the front page. Honestly thought it would probably take the blue. It strikes a very compelling--and unsettling--balance between surreal evocation and whimsical absurdity. Very distinctive artistic statement--yet one that''s elusively articulated. A chef''s kiss there.
<br/>
<br/>On a side note, I''m really interested to find out how you accomplished the levitation effect so convincingly.</td>', 'Glad to see this one on the front page. Honestly thought it would probably take the blue. It strikes a very compelling--and unsettling--balance between surreal evocation and whimsical absurdity. Very distinctive artistic statement--yet one that''s elusively articulated. A chef''s kiss there.

On a side note, I''m really interested to find out how you accomplished the levitation effect so convincingly.', '2025-10-01 13:50:46.000000', NULL, 0),
